{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the thing does not happen and does not come</b>, etc. This is when there is no repentance and good deeds that would cause HaShem to relent and withhold the punishment, as in the cases of Hezekiah and Nineveh and similar ones. Another interpretation: <b>and the thing does not happen and does not come</b>, etc. — hence it implies that it will never come. But in the portion of Re'eh it is written 'and the sign or wonder comes to pass.' One may answer that the one in the portion of Re'eh, which implies that it does come, speaks of a false prophet who was true at the outset, as explained there; while here it speaks of a false prophet from the outset."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:23.048524846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}